@startuml external-agent-onboarding
!theme plain
title External agent onboarding (v1.3): self-signed certificate, verification and pin, root-signed admission, encrypted credential package, optional workplace

participant "External agent\n(other org / machine)" as X
actor "Operator\n(or orchestrator with onboard grant\n+ operator confirmation)" as OP
participant "Trust registry\n(keys, grants, revocations)" as T
participant "Key keeper\n(root)" as KK
participant "Launch dispatcher" as D
participant "Privileged helper" as PH
participant "Bridge\n(broker, mailbox)" as BR
database "Carrier\n(Matrix / XMPP)" as MX

== 1. introduction ==
X -> X: generate key pair; self-signed certificate\n{public key, name, role, contact, validity}
X -> OP: certificate over an out-of-band channel
OP -> OP: verify the self-signature (proves key possession);\nconfirm the fingerprint over a second channel (voice, phone)
note right of OP
  MITM defence: the fingerprint is confirmed
  out of band before anything is pinned;
  every later message is signed over exact bytes.
end note
OP -> T: pin public key as external identity {name, role}
OP -> KK: sign admission record "external key K admitted with role R"
KK --> T: root-signed admission record stored

== 2. grants ==
OP -> T: grants for K: post to rooms[], read mailbox of ...,\n(optionally) session.input on a named orchestrator; expiry; delegable: no

== 3. credential package ==
OP -> OP: package {carrier endpoint, identity, rooms, tokens,\nboard endpoint and scope, our root public key, host SSH fingerprint}
OP -> X: package encrypted to K (hybrid: X25519 + AEAD), signed by the operator
X -> X: decrypt; verify the operator's signature against our root;\nconfigure its tools (mailbox client, carrier identity)
X -> MX: join rooms as the issued identity
X -> BR: first signed message "ready" (verified: signature, pin, grant)

== 4. optional workplace on our host ==
OP -> D: provision workplace for K (grant user.create)
D -> PH: create user ext_k: home, firewall (only broker + proxy; inbound SSH),\nauthorized_keys = K's SSH public key
PH --> D: uid
D -> T: bind workplace ext_k -> identity K
note right of D: see remote-workplace-attach for the connection
@enduml
